   "source": [
    "## 7. LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7.1 Rationale\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike the bag-of-words TF-IDF representation used in Section 6, a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) network consumes a sequence of word tokens **in order**, learning to integrate context across the article. This positions the LSTM between the order-agnostic classical baselines and the contextual transformer in Section 8.\n",
    "\n",
    "A **bidirectional LSTM** is used so each token sees both its left and right context simultaneously. The architecture is intentionally small (embedding dim 64, hidden dim 64, single bidirectional layer) so training remains feasible on CPU - on a GPU each epoch takes well under a minute."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f08277b7",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.019171,
     "end_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:48.058484+00:00",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:48.039313+00:00",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "### 7.2 Vocabulary and Sequence Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "The vocabulary is built from the **cleaned training text only** (token-level), capped at the 20 000 most frequent tokens with a minimum frequency of 2. Token id `0` is reserved for padding, id `1` for unknown words. Each article is truncated or padded to a fixed length of 100 tokens."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "e833f1cc",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-06-11T19:14:48.099006Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-06-11T19:14:48.098459Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.139611Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.138660Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 6.063988,
     "end_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.141567+00:00",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:48.077579+00:00",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Vocabulary size: 20,000\n",
      "LSTM batch size: 512  (auto-selected for GPU)\n",
      "Train sequences: (50496, 100)\n",
      "Test  sequences: (12625, 100)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "LSTM_MAX_LEN     = 100\n",
    "LSTM_MAX_VOCAB   = 20000\n",
    "LSTM_MIN_FREQ    = 2\n",
    "LSTM_EMBED_DIM   = 64\n",
    "LSTM_HIDDEN_DIM  = 64\n",
    "LSTM_EPOCHS      = 30\n",
    "LSTM_BATCH_SIZE  = 512 if torch.cuda.is_available() else 64\n",
    "LSTM_LR          = 1e-3\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_vocab(texts, max_vocab=LSTM_MAX_VOCAB, min_freq=LSTM_MIN_FREQ):\n",
    "    counter = Counter()\n",
    "    for text in texts:\n",
    "        counter.update(text.split())\n",
    "    vocab = {'<pad>': 0, '<unk>': 1}\n",
    "    for word, freq in counter.most_common(max_vocab - 2):\n",
    "        if freq < min_freq:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        vocab[word] = len(vocab)\n",
    "    return vocab\n",
    "\n",
    "def encode(text, vocab, max_len=LSTM_MAX_LEN):\n",
    "    tokens = text.split()[:max_len]\n",
    "    ids = [vocab.get(tok, 1) for tok in tokens]\n",
    "    ids = ids + [0] * (max_len - len(ids))\n",
    "    return ids\n",
    "\n",
    "vocab = build_vocab(X_train_text)\n",
    "LSTM_VOCAB_SIZE = len(vocab)\n",
    "print(f'Vocabulary size: {LSTM_VOCAB_SIZE:,}')\n",
    "print(f'LSTM batch size: {LSTM_BATCH_SIZE}  (auto-selected for {\"GPU\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"CPU\"})')\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_seq = np.array([encode(t, vocab) for t in X_train_text], dtype=np.int64)\n",
    "X_test_seq  = np.array([encode(t, vocab) for t in X_test_text],  dtype=np.int64)\n",
    "print(f'Train sequences: {X_train_seq.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Test  sequences: {X_test_seq.shape}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1ab8e7bf",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.021717,
     "end_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.182150+00:00",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.160433+00:00",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "### 7.3 Model Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "A single-layer bidirectional LSTM followed by dropout and a linear classification head:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Embedding(vocab_size, 64, padding_idx=0)\n",
    "    -> BiLSTM(input=64, hidden=64)        # concatenated forward + backward = 128\n",
    "    -> Dropout(0.3)\n",
    "    -> Linear(128, 1)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Output is a single logit; `BCEWithLogitsLoss` combines a sigmoid and binary cross-entropy in a numerically stable way."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "eacdfab9",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.222104Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.221377Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.671839Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.670601Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.472773,
     "end_time": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.673743+00:00",
