   "source": [
    "### 7.4 Training Loop\n",
    "\n",
    "Trained with **early stopping** on a held-out **validation split** (10 % of the training\n",
    "set). After each epoch we measure the validation loss; if it does not improve for\n",
    "`ES_PATIENCE` consecutive epochs we stop, and the **best-epoch weights are restored** before\n",
    "evaluation. The test set is *not* used to select the model or the stopping point - it is only\n",
    "tracked per epoch as a diagnostic. `LSTM_EPOCHS` is therefore an upper bound on the number of\n",
    "epochs, not a fixed count.\n",
    "\n",
    "_Note: this is the slowest cell in the notebook on CPU (roughly 5-10 minutes per epoch on the\n",
    "full ~50k train set). On a GPU each epoch is well under a minute. Reduce `LSTM_EPOCHS` or set a\n",
    "smaller `LSTM_MAX_LEN` if needed._"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "a264b31a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.749069Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-06-11T19:14:54.748242Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-06-11T19:15:16.236145Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-06-11T19:15:16.235098Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
