   },
   "source": [
    "### 10.3 Local Explanations - SHAP on the Same Articles, Across All Six Models\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the heart of the controlled comparison. We pick three representative test articles - a confidently-correct **Fake**, a confidently-correct **Real**, and the model's *most confident mistake* (echoing the error analysis in 9.3) - and explain each prediction with **the same SHAP method on every model**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every model is wrapped as a `raw text -> P(class)` function and handed to one `shap.Explainer` with a word-level **Text masker** (the model-agnostic Partition explainer). Because the masker tokenises each article on the *same* word regex regardless of model, the resulting token attributions are **directly comparable across architectures** - no stem-prefix approximation is needed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "7bc4e378",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-06-11T21:49:57.596349Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-06-11T21:49:57.595409Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-06-11T21:49:57.756409Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-06-11T21:49:57.755359Z"
    },
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.19954,
     "end_time": "2026-06-11T21:49:57.760707+00:00",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-06-11T21:49:57.561167+00:00",
     "status": "completed"
